From: Luis Guzman <ark@switnet.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:50:00 -0600
Subject: freerdp3: enable FFmpeg video decoding for GFX H.264

Ubuntu builds freerdp3 with -DWITH_FFMPEG=OFF because ffmpeg is not in
main, which also leaves GFX H.264 (AVC420/AVC444) disabled.
Clients using it, such as remmina, then fail against H.264 based rdp
servers, such as KDE krdp: authentication succeeds and the session drops
after the first frame.

---
 debian/rules | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/debian/rules b/debian/rules
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -82,7 +82,11 @@
         -DWITH_URIPARSER=OFF \
         $(empty)
 else
+    # Explicit FFmpeg video decoding enables GFX H.264 (AVC420/AVC444),
+    # required by H.264-only servers such as KDE KRdp.
     DEB_CMAKE_EXTRA_FLAGS += \
+        -DWITH_FFMPEG=ON \
+        -DWITH_VIDEO_FFMPEG=ON \
         -DWITH_GSM=ON \
         -DWITH_SWSCALE=ON \
         -DWITH_DSP_FFMPEG=ON \
